   "failure_scenario": "Linux CI runs the new timeout test, but its logging setup fails before the deliberately hanging test can start. The check exits with an ordinary failure instead of exercising the timeout, so CI fails.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: this host is macOS, so the Linux-only branch is skipped; no running Linux environment was available, and network access was prohibited.",
   "evidence": "HEAD's fixture exports `LIMITLESS_CI_TEST_LOG=\"/proc/$$/fd/2\"` inside `sh()`. That function uses `spawn` with `stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"]`; a local probe of this Bun spawn configuration reported `{\"stderrIsSocket\":true,\"stderrIsFIFO\":false}`. Linux cannot reopen such a socket through `/proc/.../fd/2` (ENXIO). The preload unconditionally calls `appendFileSync(process.env.LIMITLESS_CI_TEST_LOG, ...)`, so workers fail before reaching the hang. The wrapper's `set -eu` and `\"$@\" & wait \"$!\"` propagate that ordinary exit status; this does not establish a timeout or job-control defect. The fixture and preload logging are absent at base."
  }
